{#- testing/remote_harness/templates/lme-cold-launch-argv.json.j2 -- X2P OUTPUT `argv` (C1 s33
    external_invocation.envelope_projection.outputs.argv; the s32 generator template_rel and file name kept; codex 912 / 913
    / 914 P-B1 / 915). NEW FILE. AUTHORED, NEVER RENDERED (UNRUN). Change record: b/op1c-projector/records-b-op1c-projector-01.yml.
    OUTPUT: the exact X4 exec vector, ONE JSON list of strings: the declared launch form genesis.launch.argv
    (external_invocation.cold_launch_release.argv_from) for the X4 stage (cold_launch_release.stage), each template word
    expanded by the macro NAMED by the declared word outputs.argv.macro, reached by its declared module rel.
    HOLE-B-OP1C-ARGV-FORM (route + C1): the declared gword (route op1b genesis_entry.j2 :225-252) emits SHELL TEXT for the
    generated entry script ("$_a_<param>", "$G${_S}...", "$ACT", "$CO", "$REC", s.shq quoting), never concrete vector
    words, so it cannot produce a JSON exec vector without a false success. This template calls the named macro with the
    VALUE signature (bs, ctl, w, st, stage, rt) of the proposed shared value arm gvalue (route CPL-B-OP1C-GVALUE: the SAME
    slot dispatch as gword over launch.slots / scalar_slots / placeholder; rt is keyed by the declared placeholder TEXT
    (the launch.slots / scalar_slots values): a list-slot word -> the words rt[<its placeholder>], scalar placeholders
    replaced in place by rt[<placeholder>], literal words passed through, a placeholder with no rt entry
    -> ge.render_refuse texts.render_argv; returns JSON text of a list of strings) and C1 C1-SR328-W-ARGV-MACRO
    (outputs.argv.macro gword -> gvalue; macros_from + gvalue: [genesis, builder, checkout_members_render, macros_rel]).
    HOSTILE CHECK: every per-word result must parse to a non-mapping, non-string sequence of strings; gword's shell text
    (with the declared word still naming gword) does not, so it refuses here (texts.render_argv) -- no shell text is ever
    published as a vector. rt carries the slot values the playbook admitted (slot word -> words); the source_record slot
    carries the envelope render of THIS run (the same lookup the envelope row renders); companion -e words have no
    declared slot (CPL-SR327-ARGV-SLOT, OPEN). -#}
{#- op1d (codex 917 / route op1d SR917-RENDER-OPTIONS): rendered ONLY through N10 successor-03 in MODULE scope (the
    declared entry_generation.render options); the template vars are read from the N10 row var rh_ra_vars by the
    template_vars words. The value arm is B's vector macro (macros/cold_projection.j2), named by outputs.argv.macro
    (PROPOSED vector, C1-SR917-W-PROJECTION-MACROS); render_refuse is reached by the PROPOSED refuse_macro word. The
    stage is the X4 stage; rt carries env_pairs (genesis.launch.env) and the override slot (PROPOSED, C1-SR917-W-OVERRIDE-SLOT). -#}
{#- op1g (B; cp -n of op1f 2d1dde58, then Edit; change record b/op1g-projector/records-b-op1g-projector-01.yml; C1
    sr922b input_view.roles.argv, CPL-SR922B-B-VIEW / -B-CHECK-MACRO): bs / ctl / rt are the argv role's NARROWED view
    (rh_ra_vars); the ONE ambient read is the entry_read below (rh.controller.bootstrap.<input_view.entry_read>, also a
    member of the argv bs list). Every macro module is imported WITHOUT CONTEXT and sees only the values passed. The
    pre-substitution check is the macro NAMED by outputs.argv.check_macro (no literal template_bad); the refusal is the
    macro named by refuse_macro, reached through macros_from[refuse_macro] (render_refuse). -#}
{%- set tw = rh.controller.bootstrap.genesis.initializer.custody.external_invocation.envelope_projection.template_vars -%}
{%- set bs = rh_ra_vars[tw.bs] -%}
{%- set ctl = rh_ra_vars[tw.ctl] -%}
{%- set rt = rh_ra_vars[tw.rt] -%}
{%- set xi = bs.genesis.initializer.custody.external_invocation -%}
{%- set xp = xi.envelope_projection -%}
{%- set xr = xi.cold_launch_release -%}
{%- set cd = bs.genesis.initializer.custody.cold_launch -%}
{%- set l = bs.genesis.launch -%}
{%- set mw = namespace(v=bs, g=bs, a=bs) -%}
{%- for k in xp.macros_from[xp.outputs.argv.macro] -%}{%- set mw.v = mw.v[k] -%}{%- endfor -%}
{%- for k in xp.macros_from[xp.refuse_macro] -%}{%- set mw.g = mw.g[k] -%}{%- endfor -%}
{%- for k in xr.argv_from -%}{%- set mw.a = mw.a[k] -%}{%- endfor -%}
{%- import mw.v | relpath(xp.outputs.argv.template_rel | dirname) as cv without context -%}
{%- import mw.g | relpath(xp.outputs.argv.template_rel | dirname) as ge without context -%}
{#- op1d C1 s34 argv_slots.source_record {outputs: [envelope, companions], flag_from, form: typed_json}: the X4 source_record
    slot carries, per declared output in order, the extra_vars flag + that output's ONE typed JSON text, built HERE by the
    SAME declared macros (outputs.<role>.macro through macros_from) with the SAME runtime the envelope / companions rows
    use (no file read, no second construction); the playbook readback proves each word equals the published file text. -#}
{%- set cm = bs.source_admission.bootstrap_input.construction -%}
{%- set sr = xp.argv_slots.source_record -%}
{%- set fw = namespace(v=bs) -%}{%- for k in sr.flag_from -%}{%- set fw.v = fw.v[k] -%}{%- endfor -%}
{%- set bn = bs.source_admission.bootstrap_input.record_keys | sort | map('extract', cm.fields) | selectattr('source', 'equalto', cm.sources.binding) | map(attribute='pinned') | list -%}
{%- set bm = namespace(p=cd.initial.rows) -%}{%- for v in bn -%}{%- set bm.p = bm.p + [[v, rt[cm.sources.binding][v] | tojson]] -%}{%- endfor -%}
{%- set args = {xp.outputs.envelope.macro: [bs, xr.ingress.envelope.early_name, {cm.sources.edition: rt[cm.sources.edition] | tojson, cm.sources.digest: rt[cm.sources.digest] | tojson, cm.sources.registry: rt[cm.sources.registry] | tojson, cm.sources.launch_transport: rt[cm.sources.launch_transport] | tojson, cm.sources.binding: dict(bm.p)}],
                xp.outputs.companions.macro: [bs, {cm.sources.binding: rt[cm.sources.binding]}]} -%}
{%- set src = namespace(w=cd.initial.rows) -%}
{%- for role in sr.outputs -%}
{%- set mm = namespace(v=bs) -%}{%- for k in xp.macros_from[xp.outputs[role].macro] -%}{%- set mm.v = mm.v[k] -%}{%- endfor -%}
{%- import mm.v | relpath(xp.outputs.argv.template_rel | dirname) as om without context -%}
{%- set src.w = src.w + [fw.v, om[xp.outputs[role].macro](*args[xp.outputs[role].macro])] -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{#- op1f (codex 920 SR920_OPAQUE_ARGUMENT_VALUES; s37 genesis.launch :2300): the placeholder grammar and expansion
    completeness are checked on the TEMPLATE words (mw.a) BEFORE substitution by the module's template_bad macro; the
    substituted vector is never scanned for placeholder-shaped text (injected values are opaque and byte-preserved; the
    retired post-substitution scan refused a legitimate value holding such text). The exact tail check below and the
    projection's readback still compare the vector word for word. -#}
{#- op1h (B; cp -n of op1g 0bf807c8, then Edit; change record b/op1h-projector/records-b-op1h-projector-01.yml; C1
    sr922c CPL-SR922C-B-CHECK-IMPORT, TAKEN): the check macro is imported from ITS OWN declared module rel,
    macros_from[outputs.argv.check_macro] (s40 :1553 template_bad), WITHOUT CONTEXT, and called through that import (ck),
    never through the value module cv; at s40 both rels name the same leaf, so the import is one file read twice. The value
    macro is s40's outputs.argv.macro (vector, was gword); it is read from the declared word, never a literal. -#}
{%- set mk = namespace(v=bs) -%}
{%- for k in xp.macros_from[xp.outputs.argv.check_macro] -%}{%- set mk.v = mk.v[k] -%}{%- endfor -%}
{%- import mk.v | relpath(xp.outputs.argv.template_rel | dirname) as ck without context -%}
{%- set rtc = rt | combine({l.slots.source_record: src.w}) -%}
{%- if (ck[xp.outputs.argv.check_macro](bs, mw.a, rtc) | from_json) != cd.initial.rows -%}{{ ge[xp.refuse_macro](bs, ctl, bs.genesis.entry.texts.render_argv) }}{%- endif -%}
{%- set av = cv[xp.outputs.argv.macro](bs, mw.a, rtc) | from_json -%}
{%- if av is mapping or av is string or av is not sequence or (av | reject('string') | list) != cd.initial.rows -%}{{ ge[xp.refuse_macro](bs, ctl, bs.genesis.entry.texts.render_argv) }}{%- endif -%}
{#- the declared form ends <checkout>/<playbook> then the source_record words: exactly that tail -#}
{%- if av[(av | length) - (src.w | length) - 1:] != [rt[l.scalar_slots.checkout] ~ bs.path_admission.separator ~ rt[l.scalar_slots.playbook]] + src.w -%}{{ ge[xp.refuse_macro](bs, ctl, bs.genesis.entry.texts.render_argv) }}{%- endif -%}
{{ av | tojson }}
